---
description: Product forms use react-hook-form, Zod, and the shared Form primitives.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Forms

Use `useForm` with `zodResolver`, a Zod schema, and `Form` from `@/components/ui/form`. Do not drive form fields with `useState`. Put schemas under `src/schemas/`. Field error copy comes from `getErrorMessage(AppErrorCode...)`, not inline strings.

```tsx
// BAD
const [title, setTitle] = useState("");
<form onSubmit={save}>
  <Input value={title} onChange={(event) => setTitle(event.target.value)} />
</form>

// GOOD
const form = useForm<TaskCreateSchema>({
  resolver: zodResolver(taskCreateSchema),
  defaultValues: { title: "" },
});

<Form {...form} onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
  <FormField
    control={form.control}
    name="title"
    render={({ field }) => (
      <FormItem>
        <FormLabel>Task title</FormLabel>
        <FormControl>
          <Input {...field} />
        </FormControl>
        <FormMessage />
      </FormItem>
    )}
  />
</Form>
```
